# Line-ending policy for the whole repo.
#
# Why this file exists: the repo used to have no eol policy and `core.autocrlf=false`, so
# whatever bytes an editor wrote were the bytes that got committed. Some files ended up stored
# with CRLF and others with LF, sometimes in the same directory. Any tool that rewrote a file
# wholesale then flipped every line, turning a three-line edit into a whole-file diff that
# still built and still passed tests — so nothing caught it except review. At the worst point
# 1329 files in the working tree differed from HEAD by line endings alone.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes git normalise to LF in the index and check out LF everywhere, so a
# CRLF-writing editor no longer produces a diff at all. Binary types are listed explicitly
# rather than left to git's NUL-byte heuristic, because a false "text" guess would corrupt
# them irreversibly.

# Default: treat as text, store LF, check out LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---- Shell / tooling that MUST be LF ----
# These are executed by bash, including under WSL where CRLF gives "bad interpreter".
*.sh    text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# ---- Windows-only scripts that want CRLF ----
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# ---- Images ----
*.png  -text
*.jpg  -text
*.jpeg -text
*.webp -text
*.gif  -text
*.ico  -text
*.bmp  -text

# ---- Models / large binary data ----
*.onnx    -text
*.nnue    -text
*.tflite  -text
*.pt      -text
*.bin     -text
*.dat     -text
*.db      -text
*.pmtiles -text
# Vector tiles are protobuf, and the test fixtures are regenerated from the live archive by
# `probe_archive`. They happen to carry a NUL early enough for git's heuristic to guess binary
# today, but they also carry CRLF pairs, so a regenerated tile that guessed "text" would have
# bytes stripped and fail to decode as a protobuf error rather than a corruption.
*.mvt     -text
*.spv     -text

# ---- Archives / compressed ----
*.zip -text
*.gz  -text
*.br  -text
*.7z  -text
*.xz  -text

# ---- Native / JVM build output ----
*.so    -text
*.a     -text
*.o     -text
*.jar   -text
*.aar   -text
*.apk   -text
*.aab   -text
*.dex   -text
*.class -text

# ---- Fonts ----
*.ttf   -text
*.otf   -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
*.eot   -text

# ---- Audio / video ----
*.ogg  -text
*.mp3  -text
*.mp4  -text
*.wav  -text
*.flac -text
*.m4a  -text
*.webm -text

# ---- Office / documents ----
*.pdf  -text
*.docx -text
*.xlsx -text

# ---- Keys and certificates ----
# Certificate DER files are binary; never apply EOL (LF<->CRLF) conversion,
# which would corrupt the bytes and break TLS trust-bundle loading.
*.der      -text
*.jks      -text
*.keystore -text

# ---- Vendored CAD supplied by the part vendor ----
# LCSC's STEP/WRL models are ASCII but machine-generated and never hand-edited, so they cannot
# cause the review churn this policy exists to prevent. Excluded so they stay byte-identical to
# what the vendor shipped — normalising them would add ~460k lines of diff for no benefit.
things/hardware/scale/libs/lcsc/** -text
